1
00:00:03.464 --> 00:00:08.964
Some tenants never read email. Send them a
reminder from your own WhatsApp instead.

2
00:00:11.245 --> 00:00:16.495
The reminder is written for you: what they
owe, how many days overdue, and a link to

3
00:00:16.495 --> 00:00:17.995
their tenant portal.

4
00:00:19.708 --> 00:00:24.432
Tap send and WhatsApp opens with the chat
and message ready. You press send there —

5
00:00:24.432 --> 00:00:26.708
from your own number, nothing to set up.

6
00:00:31.385 --> 00:00:36.679
Several tenants at once? Remind on
WhatsApp takes you through them one chat

7
00:00:36.679 --> 00:00:38.179
at a time.

8
00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:45.610
No portal link yet? Create one as you send
— it's never made without you.

9
00:00:49.005 --> 00:00:53.963
Every message is logged on the tenant's
Comms tab — as a send attempt, because

10
00:00:53.963 --> 00:00:56.505
WhatsApp can't tell us it was delivered.

11
00:00:58.853 --> 00:01:04.353
No phone number, or no country code? The
button stays grey until you add one.

12
00:01:04.369 --> 00:01:08.369
That's WhatsApp reminders: written for
you, sent from your own phone.
